{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit","id":107961,"title":"Order Virtue = Bullshit!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-07T21:18:47-07:00","id":107961,"title":"Order Virtue = Bullshit!","content":"I have decided that the Order virtue is the biggest load of useless nonsense in the entire game of Scion. Almost everything your average Scion does is illegal. It doesn't matter where you are, there are probably countless laws that exist which say you cannot do the things you are trying to do. Want to swing a weapon in a public or private place you do not own? Roll your virtue. Want to use half of your purviews? Roll your virtue. Are your birth records falsified? Roll your virtue. Did you jaywalk? Roll your virtue. Did you lie about your identity to a police officer? Roll your virtue. Are you in communication with an unknown foreign entity? Roll your virtue.<br /> <br /> It's literally a fast track to nigh endless virtue extremity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T21:50:57-07:00","id":107974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit#post107961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have decided that the Order virtue is the biggest load of useless nonsense in the entire game of Scion. Almost everything your average Scion does is illegal. It doesn't matter where you are, there are probably countless laws that exist which say you cannot do the things you are trying to do. Want to swing a weapon in a public or private place you do not own? Roll your virtue. Want to use half of your purviews? Roll your virtue. Are your birth records falsified? Roll your virtue. Did you jaywalk? Roll your virtue. Did you lie about your identity to a police officer? Roll your virtue. Are you in communication with an unknown foreign entity? Roll your virtue.</div> </div> </div> </div>The vast majority of examples you list don't strike me as the kind of thing you'd encounter if you were an Orderly Scion: falsifying birth records only helps avoid official notice or commit various other types of crime; jaywalking is a crime so you just wouldn't (and unless your ST is a douche he won't punish you for such minor things); lying about your identity is only necessary if you're a criminal, which they wouldn't be.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe weapon thing, granted, that's tricky. I'd suggest that self-defense or defense of others is usually considered an exception, and you'd try to find non-illegal ways to stop what your opponent is doing. Why are you thwacking the titanspawn? Is he doing a ritual? Interrupt it by saving the sacrifice or something. Is he hurting people? Stop him in non-lethal ways, like grabbing him so his victim can run away. Stuff like that. You're a Scion, you're supposed to be clever and great: if it were easy to do the things Scions do, then Scions wouldn't need to do them because other people would. You're a hero, <i>be a hero</i>.<br /> <br /> Is it hard? Oh yes. But most virtues are supposed to be hard, if you only take ones you can easily work with or avoid then they're not really virtues, are they?<br /> <br /> And is being in contact with a foreign entity really a crime outside of China and North Korea? I've got friends all over the world, I talk to them all the time, and nobody has ever suggested that's illegal. That said, I'm in Australia, which has (for the most part) sensible laws.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T22:15:11-07:00","id":107981,"title":"","content":"The sheer quantity of laws for many places is enough to shatter the mind of your average Order scion. Since you mentioned Australia, a brief investigation of their laws reveals the following: Self defense is only an exception provided that you do not use excessive force, so you need to be certain you have the Force with Finesse knack or get lucky. The vast majority of weapons you may have as Scions would all be illegal under the majority of circumstances. Are you trespassing to stop that Titanspawn? Did you cause destruction of property? You cannot detain someone else unless they have actually committed an indictable offense, or you can prove in a court of law that someone was under threat. Are you prepared to prove to a court of law that a magic ritual was dangerous? Unless you had paperwork prior to stopping that Titanspawn, most evidence you provide is inadmissible.<br /> <br /> Your Scion may be clever, and they may be great, but keeping track of laws is more of a test for the player than the character. I propose that everyone record or notate a game of Scion. After the game, check and see how many laws you broke. If you are almost anywhere in the mortal world, you probably broke enough laws to keep you in virtue extremity for a while.<br /> <br /> It's not just hard, it's unplayable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T22:26:23-07:00","id":107983,"title":"","content":"No? It isn't? It just means you can't be a typical &quot;superhero&quot; type character that runs around doing whatever it takes to stop the bad guys. Instead you stop the bad guys by following the rules and supporting the System. Because The System Works. Report things to the police, help them do their jobs. Become a policeman. Get permits for your weapons. Don't resort to violence. Don't detain people. Or, as an alternative, change the laws. Use your Epic Charisma and Epic Manipulation to get laws that favor you passed. Reform the government. Fix corruption. Install new leaders. Create a Law Enforcement division with special powers to deal with Titanspawn and suchnot.<br /> <br /> If you want to play a more 'typical' game with face-punching, sword-waving action... don't take Order as a Virtue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T22:58:44-07:00","id":107995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=107983#post107983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No? It isn't? It just means you can't be a typical &quot;superhero&quot; type character that runs around doing whatever it takes to stop the bad guys. Instead you stop the bad guys by following the rules and supporting the System. Because The System Works. Report things to the police, help them do their jobs. Become a policeman. Get permits for your weapons. Don't resort to violence. Don't detain people. Or, as an alternative, change the laws. Use your Epic Charisma and Epic Manipulation to get laws that favor you passed. Reform the government. Fix corruption. Install new leaders. Create a Law Enforcement division with special powers to deal with Titanspawn and suchnot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did everyone at your table sign up to play this way? If not, then you need to actively block them from having their fun because it is an offense to your order. Order requires a ridiculously rigid playstyle that is mostly contingent on you being ignorant of the very laws your character is compelled to respect.<br /> <br /> That doesn't even include many places that have coercion laws that should prevent your use of many Epic Charisma and Epic Manipulation knacks. Many countries do not respect the idea of citizenship by birth, which means order breaks just being someplace without the proper paperwork, and it breaks if you do not inform the local authorities about any legendary creatures you come across. The list of laws your average Scion breaks every single game is going to be staggering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T23:49:40-07:00","id":108008,"title":"","content":"I would imagine that a Scion with Order would have to actually be aware of a law to roll if they break it.<br /> <br /> Order Scions might be invested in trying to learn as much of the law as possible, but the Virtue doesn't require you to have a law degree to know the ins and outs of the legal system. Virtues aren't enforced by some cosmic force that omnipotently knows all human laws. Virtues are things driven by the individual Scion. If there is a common misconception about the law, or a law that is simply unknown to most people, or a law that's vague, I wouldn't force a roll on a Scion with Order unless they were explicitly written as legal experts to know about all these laws.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T00:08:38-07:00","id":108011,"title":"","content":"The examples you cited are rather extreme, also. I have someone at my table who plays a high Order Scion. It just means that when the party has to do something a bit illegal, then they exclude him since he would frown on it. <br /> It seems that you and your ST should come to a happy middleground about what the limits of this are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T00:44:18-07:00","id":108022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108008#post108008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would imagine that a Scion with Order would have to actually be aware of a law to roll if they break it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be an order roll to avoid learning those laws, and gaining information about many laws is extremely easy in the information age. It is also an order roll when you find out about a law you broke, unless you turn around and march off to admit your violation and submit yourself to punishment. I suppose you could always play an order scion with 1 intelligence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108011#post108011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I have someone at my table who plays a high Order Scion. It just means that when the party has to do something a bit illegal, then they exclude him since he would frown on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chances are extremely good that character is not a frothing mess of virtue extremity because your storyteller is ignorant of most laws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2447,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","user":"TwitchTheRat","date":". 04-08-2014, 03:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T00:59:24-07:00","id":108027,"title":"","content":"Having an Order scion in your party is like having a &quot;Paladin&quot; in a party full of &quot;Rogues&quot;. There is nothing necessarily wrong with &quot;Paladins&quot;, but most players want to play like &quot;Rogues&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T01:13:00-07:00","id":108030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108022#post108022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be an order roll to avoid learning those laws, and gaining information about many laws is extremely easy in the information age.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is nothing in the write up of Order that demands being a lawyer. Hell, it doesn't even demand that your Scion obey local laws to the exclusion of all others. A Scion could hold the UN Declaration of Human Rights as superseding any local laws that don't abide, just like in the USA federal laws can trump local laws no matter what the local laws say. There is, as the write up says, &quot;...no relativism or moral ambiguity. There is only the law.&quot; A lower authority that passes laws in defiance of a higher authority is being lawless and failing to uphold the rule of law, making the Scion no longer bidden to respect their enforcers.<br /> <br /> For all you want to say other people aren't being &quot;strict enough&quot; there is just as good of a case that you're interpreting the Virtue overly strictly. This is a game. It is meant to be fun. If you find you want to reinterpret/house rule Order to be less restrictive so you can have more fun with it? Go for it. But you don't have much leg to stand on if all you're going to do is insist that your interpretation of things that aren't in the book are the solely valid interpretation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is also an order roll when you find out about a law you broke, unless you turn around and march off to admit your violation and submit yourself to punishment. </div> </div> </div>Again, it doesn't actually say this anywhere. I do agree that an Order Scion should roll or turn themselves in, but I don't see anything that says they would literally have to stop anything they're doing to turn themselves in. If an Order Scion is running across the street to save a person from being run over, but the light changes before they get all the way across, they don't have to roll to save the person before turning themselves in and insisting to the officer that they need to be ticketed for jaywalking even if it was for a good cause no matter how much the officer doesn't want to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I suppose you could always play an order scion with 1 intelligence. </div> </div> </div>You can also play a Scion with Order 1; meaning you'll fail more often than not and almost never be at serious risk of Virtue Extremity unless you're really burning through the WP (as long as you have 2 temp WP you can't suffer one).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Chances are extremely good that character is not a frothing mess of virtue extremity because your storyteller is ignorant of most laws. </div> </div> </div>Or the ST simply doesn't interpret the Virtue nearly as harshly as you're insisting is the One True Way of doing so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T03:08:44-07:00","id":108064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108030#post108030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Scion could hold the UN Declaration of Human Rights as superseding any local laws that don't abide, just like in the USA federal laws can trump local laws no matter what the local laws say. There is, as the write up says, &quot;...no relativism or moral ambiguity. There is only the law.&quot; A lower authority that passes laws in defiance of a higher authority is being lawless and failing to uphold the rule of law, making the Scion no longer bidden to respect their enforcers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree, though knowing such things requires your character to have the kind of knowledge that you are suggesting they do not need to have. Not to mention this only applies to laws that don't abide, compared to several thousand that do depending on your location.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108030#post108030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For all you want to say other people aren't being &quot;strict enough&quot; there is just as good of a case that you're interpreting the Virtue overly strictly. This is a game. It is meant to be fun. If you find you want to reinterpret/house rule Order to be less restrictive so you can have more fun with it? Go for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am absolutely and completely in favor of house ruling this wreck of a virtue into something playable.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108030#post108030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see anything that says they would literally have to stop anything they're doing to turn themselves in.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is up to the appropriate law enforcement agency to determine if she is free to continue adventuring or should be fined or incarcerated. Choosing to continue adventuring without turning herself in is selectively applying the rules to herself, even if it is only temporary.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108030#post108030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If an Order Scion is running across the street to save a person from being run over, but the light changes before they get all the way across, they don't have to roll to save the person before turning themselves in and insisting to the officer that they need to be ticketed for jaywalking even if it was for a good cause no matter how much the officer doesn't want to.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no relativism or moral ambiguity. She has to either spend a willpower or roll to save that person.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108030#post108030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can also play a Scion with Order 1; meaning you'll fail more often than not and almost never be at serious risk of Virtue Extremity unless you're really burning through the WP (as long as you have 2 temp WP you can't suffer one).</div> </div> </div> </div>There are such a mind blowing number of laws for most places, not even Order 1 is going to keep you very safe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T03:36:21-07:00","id":108072,"title":"","content":"There are also a crap-ton of laws that are not intended to be enforced, but instead are associated with other illegal activities that are harder to prove. These laws are used a a mechanism to punish the real crime when law enforcement can't prove your illegal activities. It's the reason that it's still technically illegal to have sex in any position other than Missionary in many places in the united states. The function of these laws makes it so that breaking them isn't illegal unless you're doing something else that is and thus not a problem for Order.<br /> <br /> If a behavior for a Order Scion seems absurd, it's probably because it is and you should reevaluate how your handling it. Also this is fictional earth so laws are as simple/complex as is needed to tell the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T03:50:43-07:00","id":108077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108072#post108072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The function of these laws makes it so that breaking them isn't illegal unless you're doing something else that is and thus not a problem for Order.</div> </div> </div> </div>You were doing good right up to this point. You cannot selectively enforce some laws but not others. While mortal authorities have to prioritize because the do not have the manpower or financial incentive to pursue every law, your Virtue makes no such exceptions. You either pay your willpower, or roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T04:57:06-07:00","id":108100,"title":"","content":"*shrugs*<br /> <br /> You don't need the book definition of &quot;order.&quot;<br /> <br /> Something more fluid (or so I'd think) would be to distinguish a deity's order along his/her (it?) priorities. And roll from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T06:37:45-07:00","id":108157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108077#post108077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You were doing good right up to this point. You cannot selectively enforce some laws but not others. While mortal authorities have to prioritize because the do not have the manpower or financial incentive to pursue every law, your Virtue makes no such exceptions. You either pay your willpower, or roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>You obviously have no idea the function these laws serve, or the way Order works as a virtue. Order says nothing about following the Law to the letter, and these Laws exist with an implied usage rather than a written usage. Thus it allows for Order to follow the intent of a Law rather than the explicit writing in the law, especially in cases like this where the usage and purpose is implied rather than explicit. <br /> <br /> I'm sure there are and have been cultures that don't use this method of Law, and in those cases you would have to follow what is explicitly written in those Laws. There have also been places where Law is largely arbitrary and an Order Scion would have to go along with whatever an appropriate authority tells them to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T09:53:32-07:00","id":108288,"title":"","content":"I think we're seeing the differences between &quot;Lawful Good,&quot; Lawful Neutral,&quot; and &quot;Lawful Evil.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T10:45:38-07:00","id":108333,"title":"","content":"Well then, that means that should you and your group go into someplace who has a monarchy or even a dictatorship and one in charge said &quot;You must plant a field full of potatoes under the full moon and then dance the hokey-pokey on that night while covered in lime green jello&quot; then you feel that your character should obey it since that is now The Law Of The Land and cannot be disobeyed without a Virtue roll? I mean, since you want to go with extremes, let's go to extremes, here and carry this on through to it's logical conclusion. The mean old dictator could keep giving ridiculous orders to you and you would be forced to bey each and every one of them one by one by one until you went into Virtue Extremity. <br /> Or, you could try to find a middle ground and learn the same lesson others have mentioned to you and find a middle ground and have fun with a game. <br /> Your way equals someone who either plays a hard ass and can only see the literal wording or else is that person. <br /> Not to mention, there is the Golden Rule: If story and rules come into conflict, then story wins every time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T11:07:25-07:00","id":108358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=107995#post107995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did everyone at your table sign up to play this way? If not, then you need to actively block them from having their fun because it is an offense to your order. Order requires a ridiculously rigid playstyle that is mostly contingent on you being ignorant of the very laws your character is compelled to respect.<br /> <br /> That doesn't even include many places that have coercion laws that should prevent your use of many Epic Charisma and Epic Manipulation knacks. Many countries do not respect the idea of citizenship by birth, which means order breaks just being someplace without the proper paperwork, and it breaks if you do not inform the local authorities about any legendary creatures you come across. The list of laws your average Scion breaks every single game is going to be staggering.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm in Telgar's game. My character doesn't have Order as a Virtue, but we do have a character who does. He seems to be in less trouble than the Courage characters (including mine) who feel obligated to run off and confront things all the time. Also, than the Endurance characters (including mine) who absolutely will not stop until they've accomplished their goal or something indicates the time scale has magnified. Two characters have BOTH of those, and are constantly endlessly driven to confront their problems. The Order guy has had it easy. Sometimes because we just ignore his &quot;dithering&quot; about important things (to the two of us). He stays with the two lawbreakers because of his Loyalty. It all somehow works,<br /> <br /> I'm a lawyer. I chime in when issues of when laws come into play when invited. I haven't made his life noticeably harder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T11:20:05-07:00","id":108371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108064#post108064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> She has to either spend a willpower or roll to save that person.There are such a mind blowing number of laws for most places, not even Order 1 is going to keep you very safe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless there is a law that says she has a duty to help that person that is equal to or greater than the the duty to not jaywalk. Usually affirmative obligations outweigh negative obligations. It's not hard to be the kind of person who has that duty (Good Samiritan laws, having such a relationship that not making the attempt is tortious conduct, being a person of appropriate status - emergency personnel, etc.)<br /> <br /> But you don't need to be a lawyer to make sense of it. A ST can make the determination that a law that gets in the way of the plot is superseded by another law. There is a good defense he or she can pull out of her back pocket anytime necessary in the US - a law can be Constitutionally vague enough that it's enforcement is inherently problematic and subject to too much discretion on the part of the officer making the decision. For example, a law against vagrancy that doesn't define what a &quot;vagrant&quot; is.<br /> <br /> There's also an interpretation of where the Scion is getting the urge to follow the law from. It can't be personnel knowledge. Ignorentia lex non excuse est. So it's more visceral than that. The Storyteller should be able to tell the Scion when she is about to violate the Virtue. That throws it back in the lap of the ultimate decision-maker. In my game, an Order character was trying seduce a mortal (effortlessly) and the natural consequence followed through. She met the same guy again. The first time she was in Cuba. Adultry isn't illegal. A good time was had by all. The second time, she was on a US Military base. The Uniform Code of Military Justice says adultry is illegal. She now had an Order issue.<br /> <br /> For me (and my players who all know I'm a lawyer) this is fun. For most Scion games, it's a judgment call by the ST. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T11:27:16-07:00","id":108379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108077#post108077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You were doing good right up to this point. You cannot selectively enforce some laws but not others. While mortal authorities have to prioritize because the do not have the manpower or financial incentive to pursue every law, your Virtue makes no such exceptions. You either pay your willpower, or roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you can. That latitude is actually written into most legal codes. Have your Order character become an officer of the law. Then there are a lot of things he can do as a consequence of his position. As the black-letter law with brightline definitions is the standard you're applying, there are a TON of exceptions to the duty to obey the laws based on exigent circumstances. The big one everyone knows about is self-defense. There are a lot of others. And, as I said before, the character shouldn't have to consult their inner tome of laws that apply to the place they are standing right now, they should be getting gut feeling when they are about to do something wrong (and what the right thing to do would be to a degree). So, if the ST thinks Order shouldn't apply, the character shouldn't get that gut feeling.<br /> <br /> A lot of what Scions do is exigent or even outside the bounds of the law. If something isn't addressed in the legal codes, then there is no punishment for doing it, even if it feels like there should be. (There is a very ugly case in Wisconsin involving some despicable grave-robbers that illustrates this perfectly).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 04-08-2014, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T11:35:09-07:00","id":108389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108064#post108064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I completely agree, though knowing such things requires your character to have the kind of knowledge that you are suggesting they do not need to have.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I was suggesting are not something every Scion with the Order Virtue has.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am absolutely and completely in favor of house ruling this wreck of a virtue into something playable. </div> </div> </div>Fine. Just remember that this is your opinion. This is not fact. As it should seem pretty clear, most of us don't read the Virtue as being nearly as restrictive as you do, or care nearly as much about memorizing all applicable statues in given location when we'd rather be having fun.<br /> <br /> This is a game about Titan-spawn punching heroes. It is ok to suspend a bit of disbelief regarding not being overly focused on the fine print of every law everywhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is up to the appropriate law enforcement agency to determine if she is free to continue adventuring or should be fined or incarcerated. Choosing to continue adventuring without turning herself in is selectively applying the rules to herself, even if it is only temporary.There is no relativism or moral ambiguity. She has to either spend a willpower or roll to save that person.There are such a mind blowing number of laws for most places, not even Order 1 is going to keep you very safe. </div> </div> </div>Again, this is your interpretation of the Virtue, not what the book actually says.<br /> <br /> What you're really communicating with this is not how busted Order is, but how busted you want it to be. You are choosing to interpret the Virtue in the most excessive and extreme fashion such that it becomes a train wreck to use. You can simply choose to not do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You were doing good right up to this point. You cannot selectively enforce some laws but not others. While mortal authorities have to prioritize because the do not have the manpower or financial incentive to pursue every law, your Virtue makes no such exceptions. You either pay your willpower, or roll. </div> </div> </div>Unless the law is explicitly selective as written. For example, copyright infringement is not a clear line legal standard. Nobody can know what a given ruling will be until (1) the person doing the infringing is taken to court and (2) the judge actually rules on it. This isn't a matter of human limitations, but of purposefully constructed selective judgement calls built into the law. This is not unique. Lots of laws are written where the legality of an action is purposefully unclear until a judge makes a ruling so that the judge can exercise a certain amount of leeway and selective application because the law makers wanted it that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T14:59:04-07:00","id":108620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108157#post108157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You obviously have no idea the function these laws serve, or the way Order works as a virtue. Order says nothing about following the Law to the letter, and these Laws exist with an implied usage rather than a written usage. Thus it allows for Order to follow the intent of a Law rather than the explicit writing in the law, especially in cases like this where the usage and purpose is implied rather than explicit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am afraid you are wrong. It explicitly says the opposite of what you are claiming. <i>&quot;laws must be upheld and enforced, even when their applications seem harsh or unjust.&quot;</i>, <i>&quot;there is no relativism or moral ambiguity. There is only the law.&quot;</i>, and <i>&quot;A failed Order roll allows a character to: commit a crime, turn a blind eye to a criminal act, allow a criminal to escape, bend the rules, selectively apply the rules to herself or anyone else.&quot;</i><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108371#post108371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless there is a law that says she has a duty to help that person that is equal to or greater than the the duty to not jaywalk. Usually affirmative obligations outweigh negative obligations. It's not hard to be the kind of person who has that duty (Good Samiritan laws, having such a relationship that not making the attempt is tortious conduct, being a person of appropriate status - emergency personnel, etc.)</div> </div> </div> </div>If there is a law that says you can ignore other laws in pursuit of one goal or another, then you are absolutely right. If there is no such law in in place, then you choose to spend willpower or roll Order on whichever one you are attempting to ignore. Getting into a catch-22 with your virtues, where any action you take provokes one of your virtues, is a 'feature' of the system.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108389#post108389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you're really communicating with this is not how busted Order is, but how busted you want it to be. You are choosing to interpret the Virtue in the most excessive and extreme fashion such that it becomes a train wreck to use. You can simply choose to not do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, Order as written is complete bullshit and everyone is required to turn a blind eye to countless laws, or house rule the virtue, just to make it playable. Considering the number of things that require house rules in Scion, I am beyond amused that so many people think this one is perfectly fine.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108389#post108389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless the law is explicitly selective as written. For example, copyright infringement is not a clear line legal standard. Nobody can know what a given ruling will be until (1) the person doing the infringing is taken to court and (2) the judge actually rules on it. This isn't a matter of human limitations, but of purposefully constructed selective judgement calls built into the law. This is not unique. Lots of laws are written where the legality of an action is purposefully unclear until a judge makes a ruling so that the judge can exercise a certain amount of leeway and selective application because the law makers wanted it that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you are in virtue extremity, which you probably are in quite a lot if you are playing Order as written, then you are not the judge. You need to take your infringements and violations to a local law enforcement agency, or your superior officer if you are working in such a law enforcement agency yourself, and submit yourself for judgement. It is up to them to let you off the hook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T15:29:56-07:00","id":108658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108620#post108620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there is a law that says you can ignore other laws in pursuit of one goal or another, then you are absolutely right.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you seem to be skipping in what a few people are pointing out, is that in all this massive multitude of laws most of us are theoretically under, there are legal loopholes, overriding laws, purposely built selective applications, and what-not that make the vast majority of the laws you think are making Order Scions heads explode <i>not matter</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alternatively, Order as written is complete bullshit and everyone is required to turn a blind eye to countless laws, or house rule the virtue, just to make it playable. </div> </div> </div>That is a possibility.<br /> <br /> However I find it rather unlikely given the evidence at hand. Namely what the text says, the purpose of the text, the reality of current legal processes, and an attempt to give the text a fair reading just doesn't get to the point you're clearly at. Maybe I'm missing something on the current legal reality of the world (though you haven't cited anything that gives me an particular reason to think I was ignorant of something vital). But it seems far more likely that you're being unfair in your interpretation of the text.<br /> <br /> You're the one trying to turn this into a binary situation of your interpretation as the One Correct Reading vs. everything else which is obviously ignorant of the Truth.<br /> <br /> I'm pointing out that you're skipping a lot of middle ground in how to read the text that does not result in this way of looking at it.<br /> <br /> I also think you need to consider that the point of the game is to sit down and have fun, not to waste time being angry on the Internet over something that is, at worst, you need to have tweaked a bit for you to have fun with it. Or you can just not take it, or not play with a ST that insists on running it as harshly as you think it should be read as.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Considering the number of things that require house rules in Scion, I am beyond amused that so many people think this one is perfectly fine. </div> </div> </div>This here is a bullshit argument if there ever was one. &quot;Scion has some busted parts, therefore anything I say is busted should be assumed to be busted and anyone that disagrees is being stupid because Scion clearly has busted parts.&quot;<br /> <br /> One part of the game being busted does not inherently prove any other part of the game is busted. You can be amused at it all you want, but you could also consider that you might just be wrong on this one as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unless you are in virtue extremity, which you probably are in quite a lot if you are playing Order as written, then you are not the judge. You need to take your infringements and violations to a local law enforcement agency, or your superior officer if you are working in such a law enforcement agency yourself, and submit yourself for judgement. It is up to them to let you off the hook. </div> </div> </div>1) You keep citing Virtue Extremity as being a major issue, but you need to roll more successes on a Virtue roll to resist your Virtue than you have Temporary Willpower. A low Order/high Willpower character is unlikely to tap themselves low enough on WP for this to be a problem; esp. if their Nature is easily fulfilled while in opposition to Order. Regaining WP is not difficult, as unlike many WW/OP games, there aren't any caps on it. You get it as often as you fulfill your Nature, do Spectacular deeds, or stunt and take WP as your reward. Virtue Extremities, even if a character is confronted with needing to act in opposition to their Virtues a lot, is rare unless you're not putting in effort to manage your WP.<br /> <br /> 2) Who said Order Scions can't be in a position of legal authority that gives them the legal right to make judgement calls? The Virtue never states that they must go to their superiors in such a case. If they have the legal authority to make legal calls (such as being a law enforcement officer, lawyer, or judge), then why can't they decide for themselves like non-Order individuals can?<br /> <br /> 3) You still haven't addressed that in a system the presumes innocence until guilt is proven, if guilt is not a binary legal matter (that is there is built in selective application of the law) then Order can't actually demand anything of you because you're not actually guilty of anything. In many ways, you seem to be confusing Duty and Order a bit here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T16:08:40-07:00","id":108718,"title":"","content":"Any storyteller that would make one of their players roll for jaywalking needs a bag full of D10s chucked at their forehead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2412-lucidfeverdream","name":"LucidFeverDream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T16:19:50-07:00","id":108738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108658#post108658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you seem to be skipping in what a few people are pointing out, is that in all this massive multitude of laws most of us are theoretically under, there are legal loopholes, overriding laws, purposely built selective applications, and what-not that make the vast majority of the laws you think are making Order Scions heads explode <i>not matter</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That may be the case some of the time, but certainly not all of the time. It would also vary dramatically depending on your region and the laws of that region. Furthermore, getting to that point would require exactly the kind of exhaustive knowledge of law you suggested people do not need.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108658#post108658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However I find it rather unlikely given the evidence at hand. Namely what the text says, the purpose of the text, the reality of current legal processes, and an attempt to give the text a fair reading just doesn't get to the point you're clearly at. Maybe I'm missing something on the current legal reality of the world (though you haven't cited anything that gives me an particular reason to think I was ignorant of something vital). But it seems far more likely that you're being unfair in your interpretation of the text.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then we will have to agree to disagree.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108658#post108658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think you need to consider that the point of the game is to sit down and have fun, not to waste time being angry on the Internet over something that is, at worst, you need to have tweaked a bit for you to have fun with it. Or you can just not take it, or not play with a ST that insists on running it as harshly as you think it should be read as.</div> </div> </div> </div>Declaring that everything is completely fine if you just house rule it is not very productive. I hope everyone already knows that. My goal is to convince everyone that this is one of those issues that does need to be house ruled, because Order as written is overwhelmingly restrictive. If you do not feel that way because you have a more relaxed interpretation, then as far as I am concerned you are using a house ruled version of order and I do not need to convince you of anything further.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108658#post108658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) You keep citing Virtue Extremity as being a major issue, but you need to roll more successes on a Virtue roll to resist your Virtue than you have Temporary Willpower. A low Order/high Willpower character is unlikely to tap themselves low enough on WP for this to be a problem; esp. if their Nature is easily fulfilled while in opposition to Order. Regaining WP is not difficult, as unlike many WW/OP games, there aren't any caps on it. You get it as often as you fulfill your Nature, do Spectacular deeds, or stunt and take WP as your reward. Virtue Extremities, even if a character is confronted with needing to act in opposition to their Virtues a lot, is rare unless you're not putting in effort to manage your WP.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will agree with you that you could spend a huge amount of your regained willpower resisting your Order virtue, but that is willpower that you probably hoped to be spending in other places. And if you are spending willpower to ignore your order with such astounding frequency, then wouldn't it be far more playable to simply not take Order in the first place?<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108658#post108658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Who said Order Scions can't be in a position of legal authority that gives them the legal right to make judgement calls? The Virtue never states that they must go to their superiors in such a case. If they have the legal authority to make legal calls (such as being a law enforcement officer, lawyer, or judge), then why can't they decide for themselves like non-Order individuals can?</div> </div> </div> </div>Show of hands for how many Order scions started their adventuring career with a huge amount of legal authority, or have spent the majority of their adventuring time with a huge amount of legal authority? This is a real request.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108658#post108658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) You still haven't addressed that in a system the presumes innocence until guilt is proven, if guilt is not a binary legal matter (that is there is built in selective application of the law) then Order can't actually demand anything of you because you're not actually guilty of anything. In many ways, you seem to be confusing Duty and Order a bit here.</div> </div> </div> </div>This depends entirely on the definition of 'criminal act' in any given legal jurisdiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T16:28:35-07:00","id":108748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108620#post108620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am afraid you are wrong. It explicitly says the opposite of what you are claiming. <i>&quot;laws must be upheld and enforced, even when their applications seem harsh or unjust.&quot;</i>, <i>&quot;there is no relativism or moral ambiguity. There is only the law.&quot;</i>, and <i>&quot;A failed Order roll allows a character to: commit a crime, turn a blind eye to a criminal act, allow a criminal to escape, bend the rules, selectively apply the rules to herself or anyone else.&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>That tells that don't know the meaning of those words then as none of that contradicts what I said.<br /> <br /> But I leave the arguing to the Lawyers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T17:03:07-07:00","id":108780,"title":"","content":"Well, if you want to just sit and complain, then that's your right. But since, from near I can tell, the weight of logical and empirical evidence is against you, I'm just going to file this away as &quot;someone bitching on the Internet&quot;, and afford you the appropriate amount of attention. Which is no more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T17:05:50-07:00","id":108784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108780#post108780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But since, from near I can tell, the weight of logical and empirical evidence is against you</div> </div> </div> </div>I've provided logical and empirical data, and you have not.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108780#post108780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just going to file this away as &quot;someone bitching on the Internet&quot;, and afford you the appropriate amount of attention. Which is no more.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is completely your right, and I respect your right to do so. Have a nice evening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T17:39:52-07:00","id":108806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108784#post108784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've provided logical and empirical data, and you have not.This is completely your right, and I respect your right to do so. Have a nice evening.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really really don't want to get involved in this internet fight. But all I want to say is: Do you notice that no other players/storytellers are having this issue?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2412-lucidfeverdream","name":"LucidFeverDream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T18:05:11-07:00","id":108822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LucidFeverDream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108806#post108806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really really don't want to get involved in this internet fight. But all I want to say is: Do you notice that no other players/storytellers are having this issue?</div> </div> </div> </div>I sincerely believe that most people do not realize the implications of the virtue, and do not play it as written. This is similar to how I believe most people do not realize the implications of the dying rules, and do not play them as written either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2447,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","user":"TwitchTheRat","date":". 04-08-2014, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T18:12:54-07:00","id":108827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108822#post108822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I sincerely believe that most people do not realize the implications of the virtue, and do not play it as written. Kind of like how I sincerely believe that most people do not realize the implications of the dying rules, and do not play them as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what? It still seems like you are manufacturing this problem where no one else is apparently suffering from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2412-lucidfeverdream","name":"LucidFeverDream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T18:21:05-07:00","id":108831,"title":"","content":"And that doesn't strike you, at all, as a both arrogant and amazingly dismissive of the very people you're trying to have a conversation with?<br /> <br /> Do you think people really want you to come to the forum to say, &quot;Hey you're all ignorant and not realizing how stupid this rule is even though it works just fine for you because you're not paying 100% attention to reality in a game about punching Titans!&quot;<br /> <br /> Your sincere belief that nobody else is as informed as you about something does not speak well of your position.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T18:41:57-07:00","id":108838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LucidFeverDream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108827#post108827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what? It still seems like you are manufacturing this problem where no one else is apparently suffering from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being unaware of the problem does not mean the problem does not exist. Many laws have been written or revised because someone pointed out that the way a rule is written causes more harm than good, or is not operating as intended.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108831#post108831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that doesn't strike you, at all, as a both arrogant and amazingly dismissive of the very people you're trying to have a conversation with?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108831#post108831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think people really want you to come to the forum to say, &quot;Hey you're all ignorant and not realizing how stupid this rule is even though it works just fine for you because you're not paying 100% attention to reality in a game about punching Titans!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This implies people are more interested in not being questioned, than noticing a game rule is broken and agreeing or disagreeing that it is a problem as written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T19:01:53-07:00","id":108847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108838#post108838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being unaware of the problem does not mean the problem does not exist. Many laws have been written or revised because someone pointed out that the way a rule is written causes more harm than good, or is not operating as intended.<br /> No.This implies people are more interested in not being questioned, than noticing a game rule is broken and agreeing or disagreeing that it is a problem as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>You assume that people are &quot;unaware&quot; of this. We simply don't give a damn. You should try not giving a damn. It's working out pretty well for the other 99.999% of people who play the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2412-lucidfeverdream","name":"LucidFeverDream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T19:11:28-07:00","id":108854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108838#post108838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being unaware of the problem does not mean the problem does not exist. Many laws have been written or revised because someone pointed out that the way a rule is written causes more harm than good, or is not operating as intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. Let's assume everyone acknowledges that the Order virtue, taken in the most literal interpretation, is as disruptive as you claim. You also claim that you are fine with the Order virtue being house ruled. I propose to you that everyone already <b>HAS</b> an unspoken house rule that the Order virtue should <b>NOT</b> be taken in the most literal interpretation.<br /> <br /> There is not much else to be done until the new edition of Scion is released.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T19:13:30-07:00","id":108855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108854#post108854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. Let's assume everyone acknowledges that the Order virtue, taken in the most literal interpretation, is as disruptive as you claim. You also claim that you are fine with the Order virtue being house ruled. I propose to you that everyone already <b>HAS</b> an unspoken house rule that the Order virtue should <b>NOT</b> be taken in the most literal interpretation.<br /> <br /> There is not much else to be done until the new edition of Scion is released.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Heck, the whole virtue system should be taken with a grain of salt. If abused it can outright strip most of the control and forces them to play the way the storyteller wants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2412-lucidfeverdream","name":"LucidFeverDream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T20:51:56-07:00","id":108919,"title":"","content":"I rarely post on the Scion forum, but I feel this is relevant:<br /> When I got the Hero book (wayyy back when it first came out) and read through, giddy with excitement, I got to Order, noticed that something was wrong with it, and then carried on reading.<br /> I proceeded, over the years, to notice a whole lot more wrong with Scion (some things earlier than others - lookin' your way, Epic Dex), but yes, I house-ruled Order immediately upon reading it.<br /> <br /> It was ludicrous to carry on otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T21:04:51-07:00","id":108931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108854#post108854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I propose to you that everyone already <b>HAS</b> an unspoken house rule that the Order virtue should <b>NOT</b> be taken in the most literal interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108919#post108919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I rarely post on the Scion forum, but I feel this is relevant: When I got the Hero book (wayyy back when it first came out) and read through, giddy with excitement, I got to Order, noticed that something was wrong with it, and then carried on reading.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hah! I suppose you are right. If everyone already knows that Order is broken then I suppose I am just preaching to the choir, which explains why everyone was looking at me like I was crazy. I'm just late to the party! <br /> <br /> I am sorry for all the fuss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T21:09:56-07:00","id":108936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LucidFeverDream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108855#post108855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly. Heck, the whole virtue system should be taken with a grain of salt. If abused it can outright strip most of the control and forces them to play the way the storyteller wants.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do think one of the things that Scion could have used to keep from Exalted was that characters with 1-2 dots in a Virtue shouldn't be forced to roll/spend WP in every situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T06:29:52-07:00","id":109237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108931#post108931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hah! I suppose you are right. If everyone already knows that Order is broken then I suppose I am just preaching to the choir, which explains why everyone was looking at me like I was crazy. I'm just late to the party!<br /> <br /> I am sorry for all the fuss.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nearly 3/4 of the virtues could be broken if the storyteller is a dick about their enforcement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2412-lucidfeverdream","name":"LucidFeverDream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T11:55:01-07:00","id":109506,"title":"","content":"The easiest solution to the whole situation, understanding that the laws of man do not apply to Gods and their children. Are you of a Pantheon that has order as one of its virtues? It is the laws of that Pantheon that you must obey, not the trivial laws of man which are fleeting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T14:20:08-07:00","id":109620,"title":"","content":"That is, however, a very large deviation from Order as written. It also steps on the toes of Duty and Piety a bit. Order is about putting the system over the individual because the system is what holds civilization together; not about the source of the system. <br /> <br /> I think the easiest thing is to stress that Order Scions, as idealists (the law never actually lives up to its purpose), have an ideal concept of the law that they abide by rather than worrying about the minor variations, and multitude of legal messes out there. Order Scions should be uncompromising about not subverting the rule of law, but their personal codes don't have include following ever last local law to the letter if it goes against their grander view of order. So a theocracy minded Scion can push society towards such a system without violating Order, and judges the &quot;worthiness&quot; of laws based on that theocratic mindset rather than the legal system their arose from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T17:48:29-07:00","id":109737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LucidFeverDream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=108718#post108718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any storyteller that would make one of their players roll for jaywalking needs a bag full of D10s chucked at their forehead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Challenge Accepted!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T19:25:04-07:00","id":109777,"title":"","content":"Order is about supporting <b>The System</b>. It's the idea that if you follow <b>The System</b>, it works. There are people that subvert <b>The System</b>, and people that end-run around it, or try to turn it against itself, but they're not following <b>The System</b>. If everyone just followed <b>The System</b>, life would be fine. Violence wouldn't be necessary, disagreements would be settled equitably, it'd all just be fine. It's a Virtue of ideals. That doesn't mean Scions with Order can't try to change <b>The System</b>, but it does mean they work within the law instead of attacking it from outside, or disregarding it. It's there to help!<br /> <br /> And no, it isn't about supporting your personal ethics, or your Pantheon's divine laws (but those are really important too!), its about believing that systems, ALL systems, should work. You obey your Pantheon, <i>and</i> the local mortal laws. If they're at cross purposes, try to resolve the conflict within the structures of both systems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T09:41:45-07:00","id":110122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Dude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=109506#post109506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The easiest solution to the whole situation, understanding that the laws of man do not apply to Gods and their children. Are you of a Pantheon that has order as one of its virtues? It is the laws of that Pantheon that you must obey, not the trivial laws of man which are fleeting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you saying that Scions are like Soverigns, which in this term, is anyone who believes that the civil rules of normal life don't apply to them? I could see some acting like that, but not all. I do agree that therre should be a laizze-faire approach to Order. If the person thinks that Order means obeying the law, then the player would seek to overthrow the government for all the loopholes that allow some people to legally disobey them. It would be a mess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T11:52:22-07:00","id":110197,"title":"","content":"Assuming there is a pantheon that has laws actually saying 'the Divine are not subject to the laws of man,' you could have an Order Scion that completely ignores human laws. That's kind of cheating though, and not very interesting. Piety probably represents it better too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T11:53:31-07:00","id":110198,"title":"","content":"Overthrow? No. Reform? Yes. It's amazing what a few Epic Socials on the floor of the House and Senate could do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T14:25:00-07:00","id":111761,"title":"","content":"I think you're (perhaps willfully) interpreting the Order virtue a little over-zealously. An Orderly Scion isn't Lawful Stupid -- they still have the capacity to run ethical calculi, interpret events or situations under the totality of circumstances, and consider exigencies, mitigating, and exaggerating factors.<br /> <br /> They're not going to have to roll to shirk the Order virtue to jump in front of a bus to save someone because that would constitute jaywalking. It's an exigent circumstance in which, even if you want to play rules lawyer (or lawyer-lawyer for that matter), criminal (and civil) liability is exempt under good samaritan law. In fact, in some jurisdictions a scion with Order would have to roll to shirk to <i>not</i> &quot;jaywalk&quot; because reasonably aiding others is <i>obligated by law</i>. Using a weapon in self-defense would not require an Order roll similarly, as self-defense is a mitigating circumstance. Either way, it's a petty, nitty interpretation of a Virtue which makes things incredibly difficult and annoying for the player.<br /> <br /> Ask yourself this: do you have equally-stringent interpretations of other virtues? Would a scion of the Aesir have to roll Courage to not beat down a little kid who gave them a raspberry (as that constitutes <b>A PHYSICAL CHALLENGE!</b>)? Would a scion of the Dodekatheon have to roll Vengeance to not go full-on road rage if some idiot driver merged in front of them without signalling? No? then why the blue blazes would scions with Order be treated thus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T16:51:39-07:00","id":111824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=111761#post111761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a scion of the Dodekatheon have to roll Vengeance to not go full-on road rage if some idiot driver merged in front of them without signalling?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Dodekatheon, shit I have to resist the urge to act vengefully when some ass-hat cuts me off in traffic and if anything my pasty white ass would be a Tuatha *L*<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T18:05:01-07:00","id":111841,"title":"","content":"...sheeeyeah...so true.<br /> <br /> More titan for me...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T03:26:32-07:00","id":111983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=111761#post111761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ask yourself this: do you have equally-stringent interpretations of other virtues? Would a scion of the Aesir have to roll Courage to not beat down a little kid who gave them a raspberry (as that constitutes <b>A PHYSICAL CHALLENGE!</b>)? Would a scion of the Dodekatheon have to roll Vengeance to not go full-on road rage if some idiot driver merged in front of them without signalling? No? then why the blue blazes would scions with Order be treated thus?</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not think your Courage example qualifies, because the kid is not a challenge in the slightest unless your Scion has literally no epic physicals at all. Now if that kid was a Scion with his own meaningful epic physicals? Absolutely!<br /> <br /> As for a Dodekatheon with road rage rolling vengeance? Absolutely!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T05:35:55-07:00","id":112009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=111983#post111983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not think your Courage example qualifies, because the kid is not a challenge in the slightest unless your Scion has literally no epic physicals at all. Now if that kid was a Scion with his own meaningful epic physicals? Absolutely!<br /> <br /> As for a Dodekatheon with road rage rolling vengeance? Absolutely!</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect he meant challenge in the sense of &quot;I challenge you to a duel&quot;, not challenge in the sense of &quot;this is a challenging fight&quot;. It would meet the former (in a really strict sense, which I believe is the point he's taking), but obviously not the latter","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T06:04:31-07:00","id":112019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=112009#post112009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect he meant challenge in the sense of &quot;I challenge you to a duel&quot;, not challenge in the sense of &quot;this is a challenging fight&quot;. It would meet the former (in a really strict sense, which I believe is the point he's taking), but obviously not the latter</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose you are right, which would mean the guy with Courage would have to respond to the challenge. Of course, you can be rather nice about it and gently put the kid in his place rather than exploding his skull. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T08:40:30-07:00","id":112058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=112019#post112019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose you are right, which would mean the guy with Courage would have to respond to the challenge. Of course, you can be rather nice about it and gently put the kid in his place rather than exploding his skull. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;...A failed Courage roll allows a character to: avoid the prospect of battle, resist a physical challenge, surrender to an opponent...&quot;<br /> <br /> It doesn't necessarily mean a straightforward, plainly-spoken, challenge to duel or fight. An insult or taunt, no matter how slight, can be interpreted as the prospect of battle or a physical challenge, and to let that slide means the character is shirking their virtue. Likewise with the Dodekatheon example...note <i>I</i> didn't say the driver was rudely cut off; I just said the guy merged in front without signalling, you guys <i>interpreted</i> it as such.<br /> <br /> Which was my entire point. It lies in <i>interpretation</i>. <b>Any</b> of the virtues can be interpreted to literal, purely punitive, and chronicle-derailing extremes. What the OP is doing is cherry-picking one virtue and interpreting it as that extreme, without considering the big picture or relevance to a chronicle, while making that implicit concession to all other virtues. That's extremely fallacious reasoning.<br /> <br /> Consider another example: a scion with order is in a car chase with a Titanspawn. Is that scion going to stop at every red light, stay within the lanes, signal turns, and obey each and every rule of the road? No, by no possible stretch of the imagination would they, or even could they as pursuit and deliverance of fugitives to justice is pursuit of the virtue itself (and to not, is to shirk the virtue) -- breaking lesser laws in the pursuit of the higher goal in this case is waived due to exigent circumstances. An orderly scion would certainly make every effort to limit the chaos they cause in the chase, but the higher goal always wins in the long run.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Hell, I'll throw this one in too. Scions of the Dodekatheon don't go into constant virtue extremity between black Friday and New Year's, do they. They have Vengeance, and the <i>entire holiday of Christmas is a giant fuck-you to the Dodekatheon</i>. Christmas is a fusion of Yule (a Germanic, and therefore barbarian, holiday) and Saturnalia (itself a fusion of a holiday worshipping Sol Invictus -- i.e. Akhenaten -- and Saturn -- i.e. <b>Cronus</b>), coopted by Christianity (which in the Scion world is a faith of Titanic origin). Scions of Poseidon should be especially pissed, since ancient Greek solstice celebrations were in his name which is completely forgotten in the modern day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 04-13-2014, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T10:13:15-07:00","id":112099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=112058#post112058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What the OP is doing is cherry-picking one virtue and interpreting it as that extreme, without considering the big picture or relevance to a chronicle, while making that implicit concession to all other virtues. That's extremely fallacious reasoning.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure. Do we have any proof that this is the case?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=112058#post112058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consider another example: a scion with order is in a car chase with a Titanspawn. Is that scion going to stop at every red light, stay within the lanes, signal turns, and obey each and every rule of the road? No, by no possible stretch of the imagination would they, or even could they as pursuit and deliverance of fugitives to justice is pursuit of the virtue itself (and to not, is to shirk the virtue) -- breaking lesser laws in the pursuit of the higher goal in this case is waived due to exigent circumstances. An orderly scion would certainly make every effort to limit the chaos they cause in the chase, but the higher goal always wins in the long run.</div> </div> </div> </div>Breaking one law to enforce another definitely seems like it would prompt a virtue roll, unless there are laws in place that say you are allowed to break a law to enforce another. I do not think Virtues care about your motives or your interpretation, except perhaps if you genuinely do not know. Of course, a lot of little things have to be given a pass for the sake of progress. Otherwise you wouldn't get anything done in your games!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T12:26:47-07:00","id":112169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=112099#post112099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I<br /> Breaking one law to enforce another definitely seems like it would prompt a virtue roll, unless there are laws in place that say you are allowed to break a law to enforce another. I do not think Virtues care about your motives or your interpretation, except perhaps if you genuinely do not know. Of course, a lot of little things have to be given a pass for the sake of progress. Otherwise you wouldn't get anything done in your games!</div> </div> </div> </div>There are laws in place that say you are allowed to break one law even to follow another. Self-defense for example. Defense of another for example. If we're talking enforcement, things are on even firmer ground. There are tons of laws that allow those with enforcement powers to break lesser laws for greater ones. Police cars have whirling lights on the top for just that reason. Some laws say you HAVE to come to the aid of others if it is within your power to do so. If you are not legally empowered or there is a conflict in place, it's time for a WP or a Virtue roll and you can end up cascading into Extremity. Happens with every Virtue, That's why there is the WP option. That's why there are so many ways to restore or beef-up WP compared to other WW games. <br /> <br /> Order doesn't care if you genuinely do not know a law is in place. Ignorance of the law is no excuse for breaking it. Virtues don't have anything to do with character knowledge, except in a backhanded way. The Storyteller should be telling the player that their character needs to make a Virtue roll or spend a WP when their ichor seethes because they are about to violate their Virtues. Any Virtue. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T12:47:03-07:00","id":112186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=112099#post112099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure. Do we have any proof that this is the case?</div> </div> </div> </div>Principle of exclusion. He's bringing up this one virtue, and saying it's the only one to pose such a problem. By inference, he must be making the assumption.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Breaking one law to enforce another definitely seems like it would prompt a virtue roll, <b>unless there are laws in place that say you are allowed to break a law to enforce another</b>. </div> </div> </div>Exigent and mitigating circumstances, as they're typically known. Situations in which liability for breaking one law is waived in light of the totality of circumstances, usually in the case of emergencies or enforcing/prohibiting a greater offense -- a good (non-controversial) example from US criminal procedure is that a police officer can enter a domicile without residents' permission or a warrant (therefore trespassing, and violating the 4th Amendment) if they believe the life or health of someone inside the residency is in imminent danger.<br /> <br /> In Scion terms, let's say a hungry man-eating Titanspawn has performed a home invasion and has the family tied up in the basement. Just for the sake of argument, let's say the Scions already tried to get clever and resolve the situation first without busting into the home and that failed. The would-be rescuing Scions must, by definition, trespass to save the family. Should that require an Order check? <b>absolutely not</b>, as first there's an exigent circumstance (the family is in imminent danger of being eaten) and second to allow it to happen (by action or inaction) is a direct, greater violation of Order (since the Scion would be allowing a family to be murdered and eaten, and for their captor-turned-diner to go free).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 04-13-2014, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T03:08:21-07:00","id":112514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=112186#post112186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Principle of exclusion. He's bringing up this one virtue, and saying it's the only one to pose such a problem. By inference, he must be making the assumption.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm probably getting too old these days, but I don't remember the OP saying much of anything about other virtues. Do you have a specific quote you are referencing?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=112186#post112186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Scion terms, let's say a hungry man-eating Titanspawn has performed a home invasion and has the family tied up in the basement. Just for the sake of argument, let's say the Scions already tried to get clever and resolve the situation first without busting into the home and that failed. The would-be rescuing Scions must, by definition, trespass to save the family. Should that require an Order check? <b>absolutely not</b>, as first there's an exigent circumstance (the family is in imminent danger of being eaten) and second to allow it to happen (by action or inaction) is a direct, greater violation of Order (since the Scion would be allowing a family to be murdered and eaten, and for their captor-turned-diner to go free).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not the smartest person around, but I think you are agreeing with me? I'm honestly not sure. Basically if you know the law says you can break other laws to save someone, then Order will let you do it. If you know there is no law that allows you to break the law to save someone, then Order will not let you do it.<br /> <br /> But Order is not omniscient. If you don't know about the existence of a law then you would not need to roll Order Alternatively, if you think a law exists that prevents you, then you would definitely need to roll Order. Either way you would need to roll Order once you found out that you were ignorant or mistaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1505,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","user":"Charles Red","date":". 04-14-2014, 06:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T03:29:34-07:00","id":112518,"title":"","content":"There are two different opinions on virtue going one here. Some think it is an outside force that acts upon the character through their Legend. Others think it is an inherent personality trait, part of the character. The first would make it an omniscient force informing the character if they are about to break a law, the second would make to based on character knowledge and probably make it so the the character must devote a significant portion of time to the study of law.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T03:38:39-07:00","id":112521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=112518#post112518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are two different opinions on virtue going one here. Some think it is an outside force that acts upon the character through their Legend. Others think it is an inherent personality trait, part of the character. The first would make it an omniscient force informing the character if they are about to break a law, the second would make to based on character knowledge and probably make it so the the character must devote a significant portion of time to the study of law.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I actually land somewhere in the middle.<br /> <br /> I definitely do not think virtues are... a completely external force. That would give them properties that might not be balanced, like the ability to know if a law exists because you tried to do something and Order would not let you. Or the ability to know art exists in a building you have never been inside with Expression. Or the ability to know someone broke divine law when you have never met them or heard about them with Vengeance.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I do not think virtues are personifications of your personality. Some of the greatest characters I have ever seen played were ones who struggled with their virtues because those virtues were more than the personality of the character. A cowardly man who has to cope with huge amounts of courage, a shy person who finds themselves with enormous amounts of expression, or even someone who preaches intolerance finding themselves unable to censor debate anymore.<br /> <br /> I guess that makes it like a biological response?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1505,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","user":"Charles Red","date":". 04-14-2014, 06:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T06:59:15-07:00","id":112604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=112514#post112514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm probably getting too old these days, but I don't remember the OP saying much of anything about other virtues. Do you have a specific quote you are referencing?<br /> I'm not the smartest person around, but I think you are agreeing with me? I'm honestly not sure. Basically if you know the law says you can break other laws to save someone, then Order will let you do it. If you know there is no law that allows you to break the law to save someone, then Order will not let you do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm saying the argument is a complete non-starter, as even under the strictest-possible interpretation of order, these legal principles already exist in most jurisdictions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T11:09:36-07:00","id":112784,"title":"","content":"It's taking the topic in a new direction, but it's my belief that the Virtues are bound to the Scion by his relation to his pantheon. I think extrinsic vs. intrinsic doesn't really work as a way to describe them. Intrinsic - sure. &quot;The ichor seethes&quot;. Sounds pretty damn intrinsic. Extrinsic - even more important. Virtues should not be subject to the whims of the character. It's not what I have Conviction in, it's what the Aztec gods have Conviction in - the need to keep the universe going by oiling the gears with the blood of sacrifice. Which can demand some things that are pretty damn unappealing to modern sensibilities. Which is different than what the Egyptian gods have Conviction in - keeping to the universal principles of Ma'at. Which is more in line, but can lead to some serious issues as well. (Just not so bloody in most cases). I can't be an Aztec Scion and opt into the Egyptian world view anymore than I can be an Egyptian Scion and opt into the Aztec one. I certainly can't substitute my own belief structure. In some cases my belief structure can inform my Conviction, but it can't replace or even modify it substantially. It's pretty much always about what the Virtue is about, not me. Otherwise, why even have them? They aren't constraints at all. I will deliberately keep myself ignorant of the law to insure that I deal with Order as little as possible. Etc. Etc. <br /> <br /> I don't have an issue with people using their Virtues to test their surroundings. Why not? Is that building full of art. Dunno. I'll start putting together a plan to torch it. OUCH! There goes my Expression. Even though I'm getting a warm fuzzy feeling from my Intellect. Is it breaking the law to do X? Start doing X and see if your Order goes off. Those would be brilliant out of the box uses of the Virtues. I'd applaud the PC who thought of it and probably give them a stunt for it. Does it imbalance the game at all? If so not very much. How useful is it to keep trying more and more different things to suss out the local law code? It's trying to prove a negative and it's effectively endless with no real way to achieve your desired outcome. Reminds me of a villain from the weird Vertigo Doom Patrol days. He had every power you never thought of. So people start the fight listing the standards - flight, superstrength, etc. His first move - &quot;You didn't think of the power to trap negative energy entities in glass bottles&quot;. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T16:50:27-07:00","id":113012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=112784#post112784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's taking the topic in a new direction, but it's my belief that the Virtues are bound to the Scion by his relation to his pantheon. I think extrinsic vs. intrinsic doesn't really work as a way to describe them. Intrinsic - sure. &quot;The ichor seethes&quot;. Sounds pretty damn intrinsic. Extrinsic - even more important. Virtues should not be subject to the whims of the character. It's not what I have Conviction in, it's what the Aztec gods have Conviction in - the need to keep the universe going by oiling the gears with the blood of sacrifice. Which can demand some things that are pretty damn unappealing to modern sensibilities. Which is different than what the Egyptian gods have Conviction in - keeping to the universal principles of Ma'at. Which is more in line, but can lead to some serious issues as well. (Just not so bloody in most cases). I can't be an Aztec Scion and opt into the Egyptian world view anymore than I can be an Egyptian Scion and opt into the Aztec one. I certainly can't substitute my own belief structure. In some cases my belief structure can inform my Conviction, but it can't replace or even modify it substantially. It's pretty much always about what the Virtue is about, not me. Otherwise, why even have them? They aren't constraints at all. I will deliberately keep myself ignorant of the law to insure that I deal with Order as little as possible. Etc. Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly what I was talking about earlier when I was saying that while the OP was making a reference to Order and using modern laws as the focal point of the Virtue, I was saying that for a Scion of a Pantheon who follows Order, it would be in relation to the Order as their pantheon sees it. Modern laws change on almost a daily basis, and the ancient gods are not going to adhere to anything that is not in fitting with their view of the world. <br /> <br /> Example: Despite any laws relating to the interment or use of human remains, I highly doubt a Loa is going to conform to these laws considering the fact that Bokor (The religion of those who serve the Loa) has many examples of the creation of Zombies. In fact if anyone were to think &quot;Which Pantheon are Zombies most associated with&quot; 9 times out of 10 the Loa would be the one pointed to. But the Loa follow the virtue of Order so this would be a conflict of a very well known part of the Pantheon vs Modern Law. <br /> <br /> Hence my argument that the view of each virtue is not bound by the mortal world or human law, but the much older and more stable view of how that particular pantheon views the virtues.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T17:31:45-07:00","id":113031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=112784#post112784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not what I have Conviction in, it's what the Aztec gods have Conviction in - the need to keep the universe going by oiling the gears with the blood of sacrifice. Which can demand some things that are pretty damn unappealing to modern sensibilities. Which is different than what the Egyptian gods have Conviction in - keeping to the universal principles of Ma'at. Which is more in line, but can lead to some serious issues as well. (Just not so bloody in most cases). I can't be an Aztec Scion and opt into the Egyptian world view anymore than I can be an Egyptian Scion and opt into the Aztec one. I certainly can't substitute my own belief structure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well you could if you really wanted, but your parents would be rather upset with you. To be fair, Conviction is kind of a sticky virtue because it does not clearly indicate what it is doing. Your example about the Aztecs is more like Duty, and your example with the Egyptians is more like Harmony and Order. But Conviction... can theoretically make you adhere to your other virtues more strongly. Unless you go with the &quot;Conviction is whatever I want&quot; interpretation, which is even more sticky and strange.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=112784#post112784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will deliberately keep myself ignorant of the law to insure that I deal with Order as little as possible. Etc. Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would make a player roll Order if he was intentionally avoiding learning local laws.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=112784#post112784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have an issue with people using their Virtues to test their surroundings.</div> </div> </div> </div>It certainly has some very fascinating and interesting implications. Either way, it keeps the game running smoother if Virtues are at least somewhat internal. The biological comparison someone made earlier is a fairly good representation.<br /> <b>Virtues react to what you know, but not to what you think.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T20:39:47-07:00","id":113103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=112784#post112784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's taking the topic in a new direction, but it's my belief that the Virtues are bound to the Scion by his relation to his pantheon. I think extrinsic vs. intrinsic doesn't really work as a way to describe them. Intrinsic - sure. &quot;The ichor seethes&quot;. Sounds pretty damn intrinsic. Extrinsic - even more important. Virtues should not be subject to the whims of the character. It's not what I have Conviction in, it's what the Aztec gods have Conviction in - the need to keep the universe going by oiling the gears with the blood of sacrifice. Which can demand some things that are pretty damn unappealing to modern sensibilities. Which is different than what the Egyptian gods have Conviction in - keeping to the universal principles of Ma'at. Which is more in line, but can lead to some serious issues as well. (Just not so bloody in most cases). I can't be an Aztec Scion and opt into the Egyptian world view anymore than I can be an Egyptian Scion and opt into the Aztec one. I certainly can't substitute my own belief structure. In some cases my belief structure can inform my Conviction, but it can't replace or even modify it substantially. It's pretty much always about what the Virtue is about, not me. Otherwise, why even have them? They aren't constraints at all. I will deliberately keep myself ignorant of the law to insure that I deal with Order as little as possible. Etc. Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's some wiggle room with Conviction... I think Conviction is a collection of a lot of smaller convictions (note the capitalizations), some of which are extrinsic, some are intrinsic. Conviction is about knowing what's important to you, believing with all your heart that they must be upheld, and not stopping no matter what obstacles there may be. So, in the Aztec vs. Egyptian hypothetical, I agree that, yes, upholding Ma'at and performing blood sacrifice are all Convictions that, upon visitation, every Scion of those pantheons should have thrust upon them. <br /> <br /> But let's expand this hypothetical: Two Scions are visited, and the two of them have been working for an organization to stamp out hunger, and since before their Visitation, they believe with all their might that they need to feed the poor and the downtrodden. One of these Scions is Aztec, the other is Egyptian. In addition to their unique Pantheon convictions, their Conviction Virtue would reinforce the &quot;feed the hungry&quot; conviction they already share (and that they will certainly use their newfound powers to fulfill). <br /> <br /> Conviction is a difficult virtue...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T14:41:48-07:00","id":113568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>griffinguy24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=113103#post113103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think there's some wiggle room with Conviction... I think Conviction is a collection of a lot of smaller convictions (note the capitalizations), some of which are extrinsic, some are intrinsic. Conviction is about knowing what's important to you, believing with all your heart that they must be upheld, and not stopping no matter what obstacles there may be. So, in the Aztec vs. Egyptian hypothetical, I agree that, yes, upholding Ma'at and performing blood sacrifice are all Convictions that, upon visitation, every Scion of those pantheons should have thrust upon them.<br /> <br /> But let's expand this hypothetical: Two Scions are visited, and the two of them have been working for an organization to stamp out hunger, and since before their Visitation, they believe with all their might that they need to feed the poor and the downtrodden. One of these Scions is Aztec, the other is Egyptian. In addition to their unique Pantheon convictions, their Conviction Virtue would reinforce the &quot;feed the hungry&quot; conviction they already share (and that they will certainly use their newfound powers to fulfill).<br /> <br /> Conviction is a difficult virtue...</div> </div> </div> </div>And probably not the best example to use in a discussion about Order, admittedly. For example, an Aesir Scion who switches out for Conviction might have some very weird ideas about Ragnarok... such as actively working to bring it about if the appropriate events are unfolding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T14:50:35-07:00","id":113574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=113031#post113031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Virtues react to what you know, but not to what you think.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I guess this where we disagree. To me, Virtues don't react to what you think and they don't react to what you know, they react to what IS. A Scion is as much a vehicle of his/her Virtues as you and I are of our genetic code. That's not to say that all the Scion is is a bundle of his/her pantheon's Virtues as perpetuated generation after generation via ichor, anymore than a human is a bundle of genetic traits. <br /> <br /> With that in mind, as a Storyteller, I don't have to worry about whether or not a Scion goes out of their way to read up on the local laws every time he or she changes jurisdictions (which is pretty much every time there's a change of local ordinances, perhaps even neighborhood association rules or bylaws of the group meeting). She'll just KNOW she's in danger of doing the unlawful thing and 1) choose not to do it (or do it, depending on the law in question), 2) roll the Virtue and let her ichor decide her action or 3) pay the Willpower. <br /> <br /> Though now I love the idea of the Order Scion completely ENRAGED that the house down the street is painted RED when the association rules clearly say that's a violation. In a very goofy comedy game of Scion... <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T15:31:18-07:00","id":113591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=113574#post113574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess this where we disagree. To me, Virtues don't react to what you think and they don't react to what you know, they react to what IS. A Scion is as much a vehicle of his/her Virtues as you and I are of our genetic code.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is perfectly fair. Just make sure you are not reducing the importance of Academics, Occult, Politics, Justice(Judgement), and Mystery. Allowing virtues to gather information the Scion did not already know means those abilities are less valuable.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=113574#post113574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With that in mind, as a Storyteller, I don't have to worry about whether or not a Scion goes out of their way to read up on the local laws every time he or she changes jurisdictions (which is pretty much every time there's a change of local ordinances, perhaps even neighborhood association rules or bylaws of the group meeting). She'll just KNOW she's in danger of doing the unlawful thing and 1) choose not to do it (or do it, depending on the law in question), 2) roll the Virtue and let her ichor decide her action or 3) pay the Willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're actually creating more work for yourself. If Virtues are omniscient, then it is necessary for you to go down a mental checklist of the virtues in your party during each and every situation in a given scene. You lose the ability to delegate most of that responsibility to your players, because omniscient Virtues are based on knowledge the players do not possess. This is definitely your prerogative to choose, of course!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T16:06:38-07:00","id":113614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=113591#post113591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're actually creating more work for yourself. If Virtues are omniscient, then it is necessary for you to go down a mental checklist of the virtues in your party during each and every situation in a given scene. You lose the ability to delegate most of that responsibility to your players, because omniscient Virtues are based on knowledge the players do not possess. This is definitely your prerogative to choose, of course!</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, a Storyteller should know which Virtues his players characters possess and keep an eye open for them being in violation of them anyways so he can know when to make them roll or not. So it's just a matter of continuing to do what he should already be doing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T16:55:37-07:00","id":113653,"title":"","content":"I have a cheat sheet. With all the characters and NPCs involved in that session. It's not at all hard to keep track of and not even a appreciable amount of work in a game with this kind of combat.<br /> <br /> My characters also play their Virtues too. Often more extreme than I would have asked them too if I had been playing Jiminy Cricket on their shoulder. (I do the same thing as a player. I know my Storyteller wishes I would dial back on what I feel is necessary to Courage... For him, it's the situation in front of you. For my character, it's when there's &quot;a fight worth fighting&quot;)<br /> <br /> To judge by the amount of Academics, Occult, etc roles my players end up making at my instigation or their requests, I don't think I've minimized the value of those Abilities. They keep buying more and more of them in a game where Ability and Attribute points are effectively non-important compared to the Epics. In fact, I may have enhanced them as using the 'omniscient' aspect of the Virtue as a great incentive for an obvious good use of a Virtue Channel. <br /> <br /> As I previously stated, using a Virtue to figure things out is a lot less efficient than using the relevant Ability. Trying to figure out a legal code by initiating every action you think might be illegal to see which one makes your Order twinge is not very efficient when compared to using Politics or Academics to see if the character already knows it or what they can find out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T20:07:27-07:00","id":113763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Dude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=113614#post113614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really, a Storyteller should know which Virtues his players characters possess and keep an eye open for them being in violation of them anyways so he can know when to make them roll or not. So it's just a matter of continuing to do what he should already be doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's always a good idea to keep an eye open in case one of your players forgets that their virtue might apply in a situation. But that is a task better delegated to the players, who can often be harder on themselves than you! Your focus is usually better spent on the story and NPC interactions.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=113653#post113653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a cheat sheet. With all the characters and NPCs involved in that session. It's not at all hard to keep track of and not even a appreciable amount of work in a game with this kind of combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it really comes down to whether or not your players have more fun with an omniscient virtue system, a biological virtue system, or a mental virtue system. As long as you have tried them all, I suppose it does not matter if the omniscient virtue system takes more effort or not as long as everyone is having more fun than the alternative.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=113653#post113653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To judge by the amount of Academics, Occult, etc roles my players end up making at my instigation or their requests, I don't think I've minimized the value of those Abilities</div> </div> </div> </div>I've given it a lot of thought, and I think we may have to agree to disagree on this point. I cannot see a way where it does not objectively diminish the value of those skills. But if your players do not notice that reduction (from my perspective), and they are still totally happy with those skills and purviews, then you keep on rocking what works for your group! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T09:16:23-07:00","id":114124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=113763#post113763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's always a good idea to keep an eye open in case one of your players forgets that their virtue might apply in a situation. But that is a task better delegated to the players, who can often be harder on themselves than you! Your focus is usually better spent on the story and NPC interactions.<br /> I guess it really comes down to whether or not your players have more fun with an omniscient virtue system, a biological virtue system, or a mental virtue system. As long as you have tried them all, I suppose it does not matter if the omniscient virtue system takes more effort or not as long as everyone is having more fun than the alternative.<br /> I've given it a lot of thought, and I think we may have to agree to disagree on this point. I cannot see a way where it does not objectively diminish the value of those skills. But if your players do not notice that reduction (from my perspective), and they are still totally happy with those skills and purviews, then you keep on rocking what works for your group! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I completely disagree with handing decisions about Virtues over to players. That doesn't work with the way I see Virtues, character management, player involvement, game balance, having the Storyteller do his/her job or even role-playing in general. I don't know whether you have experienced full on power gamers and rules lawyers or &lt;shudder&gt; the dreaded combination of two, but I have for over three decades. And they have often been close friends. Using the rules to keep the game on an even keel is not handling my tasks as Storyteller incorrectly. I have players who have played with me for literally decades. Sometimes even these players, even the ones who are not power gamers or rules lawyers, end up trying to maximize the power and ability of their character vis-a-vis a situation they encounter beyond their limitations. That's one of the reasons the rules are there. Even in games like Amber Diceless, where it is possible to say, &quot;my character can do anything, so she does X&quot; there are rules that allow for adjudicating character to character and character to NPC and character to setting interaction. Virtues are definitely an important way of doing so in Scion. Enforcing adherence to Virtues is pretty much the same as enforcing the consequences of taking damage. To me, it's a fundamental part of Scion and should be handled that way. I trust my players to play their characters. They trust me to run the game. Virtues are a limitation that also provide some occasional advantage. I don't ask my character's to work hard at limiting their characters, I'll do that in 1000s of ways. I want them to have fun playing their characters within the constraints of the environment. If they want to overburden themselves with how they play their Virtues, I'm cool with that. I don't demand it. But making sure that, in the heat of the great idea, the guy with Order is okay with killing a cop as part of the plan realizes that he's about to do something against the very core of his bring? That's MY job. <br /> <br /> If I my players are investing heavily in the &quot;disadvantaged&quot; Abilities and I regularly call for rolls of those abilities, then with regard to my game, the use/purchase of Abilities and the way Virtues are handled, empirically, those Abilities are not disadvantaged. Just because the same effect can be gained in an alternate way does not diminish the usefulness in gaining that effect through a better, cheaper and more efficient way. Analogies - It's not the same to pull out your handy well-honed knife to cut a slice of bread as it is to stand in a dark room in which somewhere, there is a table and somewhere on that table, there is a loaf of bread and you have to use your dull skewer and randomly stab around trying to cut the bread. I can use the handle of screwdriver as a hammer, but, man, I'd rather use a hammer; I'll use the screwdriver if that's all I've got, but I won't expect it to work as well as a hammer. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T18:30:06-07:00","id":114454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=114124#post114124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I completely disagree with handing decisions about Virtues over to players.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is the end of the discussion. I deeply appreciate you taking the time to write the rest of your post, but the conversation feels like it has turned antagonistic and defensive. I have no desire to compare the length of our storyteller cocks. If you feel that I was the one who started it, then I am genuinely sorry for giving you that impression. <b>Have a great night.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 04-16-2014, 09:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T23:47:44-07:00","id":114579,"title":"","content":"I've pretty much entirely done away with the normal virtues system, and replaced it with something resembling FATE's aspect system. It's worked out pretty well for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T00:22:09-07:00","id":114585,"title":"","content":"It's really amazing how everything turned out because... the rat doesn't feel concerned anymore for about 2 pages and we'll still arguing... or whatever the verb you feel like replacing arguing.<br /> Anyway, one of players asked me about the Virtues' issues, not just about Order. They are all supposed to play criminals and he asked me how they were supposed to be criminals and heroes at the same time. How criminals could have any Scion Virtue? I just told him that besides Order, other Virtue is really okay. Besides, even superheroes aren't totally virtuous. Maybe Captain America is the only one. He understood what I meant and it wasn't an issue anymore.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T00:52:34-07:00","id":114588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=114585#post114585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, one of players asked me about the Virtues' issues, not just about Order. They are all supposed to play criminals and he asked me how they were supposed to be criminals and heroes at the same time. How criminals could have any Scion Virtue? I just told him that besides Order, other Virtue is really okay. Besides, even superheroes aren't totally virtuous. Maybe Captain America is the only one. He understood what I meant and it wasn't an issue anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>While virtues are certainly &quot;disruptive&quot; they are not necessarily good or evil in any sense of the world. They influence your behavior along certain paths, but it is entirely possible to do genuinely heinous things with all of the virtues. Even Order. Order just lends itself to lawful exploitation, malevolent governments, and class systems.<br /> <br /> By a strict definition I suppose that does not make you a criminal, but more like a 'Politician' or 'Donald Trump'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T05:38:26-07:00","id":114669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=114585#post114585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's really amazing how everything turned out because... the rat doesn't feel concerned anymore for about 2 pages and we'll still arguing... or whatever the verb you feel like replacing arguing.<br /> Anyway, one of players asked me about the Virtues' issues, not just about Order. They are all supposed to play criminals and he asked me how they were supposed to be criminals and heroes at the same time. How criminals could have any Scion Virtue? I just told him that besides Order, other Virtue is really okay. Besides, even superheroes aren't totally virtuous. Maybe Captain America is the only one. He understood what I meant and it wasn't an issue anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bear in mind, players don't have to put dots in a given virtue. They can even swap that given virtue out for one more befitting, if they feel it's appropriate.<br /> <br /> I'm playing a scion of Loki currently, who is a con man that prefers to talk or think his way out of situations rather than bash in skulls. If I had chargen to do all over again I'd have swapped Courage for Intellect, but I didn't at the time -- instead I just left Courage at 2 and loyalty at 1. Courage means you face your enemies and face them alone...doesn't mean you face them fair and square, or check your common sense at the door facing them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T06:51:59-07:00","id":114690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=114588#post114588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While virtues are certainly &quot;disruptive&quot; they are not necessarily good or evil in any sense of the world. They influence your behavior along certain paths, but it is entirely possible to do genuinely heinous things with all of the virtues. Even Order. Order just lends itself to lawful exploitation, malevolent governments, and class systems.<br /> <br /> By a strict definition I suppose that does not make you a criminal, but more like a 'Politician' or 'Donald Trump'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Think about following your Order Virtue in Nazi Germany.... or think about NOT following it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T08:10:18-07:00","id":114716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=114690#post114690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think about following your Order Virtue in Nazi Germany.... or think about NOT following it</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very good example!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T12:35:55-07:00","id":117100,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's the min-maxer in me... maybe it's the fact that I've been a Storyteller for practically my entire gaming career... but it seems to me that if you have a problem with Order, follow the KISS (Keep It Simple Stupid) method:<br /> <br /> You have 5 virtue points to spend at character creation. If you have Order, keep it at one dot and fail away at the roll. If you're rolling rather lucky (or unlucky in some cases), spend the willpower. OR... <i>Hero</i> has a wonderful sidebar detailing the possibility of taking alternate virtues. So long as your Storyteller is willing, go with a different virtue that could work instead. Vengeance or Intellect or Courage... seriously It's not that complicated. Maybe it will cause some strife with your parent pantheon. That's good roleplay value. And it might get you in better with pantheons that have the virtue you took instead.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I have no need of putting in my two cents worth. Plenty of people have already explained to death what Order is. If there was something I thought I could add, it'd be along the lines of &quot;Order is meant to prevent chaos and anarchy, whilst Duty is the drive to follow.&quot; Order can be subjective. If a criminal is getting away with something like murder because the law's too lenient (not because of a loophole or anything), then Order claims he needs to be punished. It's the overlap of Duty and enforcing Order that seems to be the big argument overall. To keep it simple for me, I view Order as the knowledge and Duty as the action. While Order requires some acts, it relies on the basis of knowing that what you're doing is right, whereas Duty relies on (hopefully) believing that what you're doing is right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1545-aodhstormeyes","name":"aodhstormeyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T13:53:17-07:00","id":117142,"title":"","content":"The only way someone can &quot;get away&quot; with murder as far as Order is concerned is if they committed that crime and were not punished for it. As long as there is no violation of the system, that person did not commit murder, they lawfully ended the life of another. Which means, under the legal systems most of us live under, a character laboring under Order cannot kill someone they know killed another until that person is actually found guilty by an appropriate authority and then said authority gets to designate the lawful punishment. <br /> <br /> No matter how much you KNOW he did it, you're going to have to let the system do it's job. Or fail a roll/spend a WP. <br /> <br /> Living with the ugly side of Virtues is part of the time. You're right. Take a 1 or switch it out (if you're allowed and are willing to accept whatever your Storyteller intuits the penalties might or might not be for doing so). <br /> <br /> Even 1's can suck. I had a character roll on Intellect 1 and make the roll and he had to go with a plan that everyone else had abandoned. Since they abandoned it for no plan at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T21:11:02-07:00","id":117382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=117142#post117142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even 1's can suck. I had a character roll on Intellect 1 and make the roll and he had to go with a plan that everyone else had abandoned. Since they abandoned it for no plan at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>1's are more disruptive than the 4's and 5's. You chose to give yourself 4's and 5's. The personality of your character is built around those big virtues more often then not, and you know you are almost always going to roll successes on them. So you can almost always calculate when you want to go with it, and when you want to resist.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut 1's suck up just as many willpower points to resist as 4's and 5's, and you are far more likely to gamble with them in the hopes that you will roll no successes. Which means you lose that gamble more frequently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T22:14:30-07:00","id":117413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=117382#post117382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1's are more disruptive than the 4's and 5's. You chose to give yourself 4's and 5's. The personality of your character is built around those big virtues more often then not, and you know you are almost always going to roll successes on them. So you can almost always calculate when you want to go with it, and when you want to resist.</div> </div> </div> </div>While you literally have a guillotine hanging over your neck forcing you to take Virtues you don't like? Shouldn't <i>all</i> Virtues only be taken because they suit your character?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T22:52:56-07:00","id":117429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=117413#post117413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While you literally have a guillotine hanging over your neck forcing you to take Virtues you don't like? Shouldn't <i>all</i> Virtues only be taken because they suit your character?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a question with lots of differing opinions in the Scion fandom (which, honestly, can be said for <i>any</i> question in the Scion fandom). It depends on if you think Virtues are a representation of a <b><i>character's</i></b> deeply held beliefs that are <b><i>enhanced</i></b> by ichor, or if they are a representation of the <b><i>Pantheon's</i></b> deeply held beliefs and are <b><i>imposed</i></b> by ichor. If the former, then Scions should definitely only pick the Virtues they feel their character should have. If you hold the latter view, on the other hand, then Virtues are more akin to control chips in your brain and you don't have any more choice than a Vampire has a 'choice' to not burn in the sun. I have seen most people go with a compromise of Three Pantheon Plus One Character Virtues, with or without XP penalty on your PSP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T00:43:38-07:00","id":117461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=117142#post117142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only way someone can &quot;get away&quot; with murder as far as Order is concerned is if they committed that crime and were not punished for it. As long as there is no violation of the system, that person did not commit murder, they lawfully ended the life of another. Which means, under the legal systems most of us live under, a character laboring under Order cannot kill someone they know killed another until that person is actually found guilty by an appropriate authority and then said authority gets to designate the lawful punishment.<br /> <br /> No matter how much you KNOW he did it, you're going to have to let the system do it's job. Or fail a roll/spend a WP.<br /> <br /> Living with the ugly side of Virtues is part of the time. You're right. Take a 1 or switch it out (if you're allowed and are willing to accept whatever your Storyteller intuits the penalties might or might not be for doing so).<br /> <br /> Even 1's can suck. I had a character roll on Intellect 1 and make the roll and he had to go with a plan that everyone else had abandoned. Since they abandoned it for no plan at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I was stretching for an example with that, but you got the basic point. Basically I was thinking of instances where a person gets practically no punishment for a crime that the law states they should get something akin to life in prison (and their punishment is literally not even considered to be near the minimum punishment). My wording usually gets screwed up on the way out of my mouth... or fingers in this case.<br /> <br /> And yeah. With my current game, I've got two Chinese Scions, a Persian Scion, and a Deva Scion. All of them have virtues like Order and Harmony at 1. I didn't allow them to change out a virtue (since it's my first game), and they've done great at showing things like Valor, Intellect, or Endurance. But this topic has gotten me to thinking about how their &quot;less important&quot; virtues will affect them. Obviously, I prefer a loose reading on Virtues, playing the wordsmith if it seems to fit with a definition of the Virtue.<br /> <br /> Though to be honest, one of the Chinese scions tried sniping a werewolf as a surprise attack. The guy paid a Willpower since his Valor is 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1545-aodhstormeyes","name":"aodhstormeyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T18:02:26-07:00","id":117757,"title":"","content":"We had a Son of Artemis Scion who was an marine corps sniper in one of our Scion games. He had Valor 1. Whenever he wanted to use his snazzy Relic sniper rifle, he rolled Valor, if he made the role, he gave them a warning shot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T08:28:45-07:00","id":125187,"title":"","content":"Interesting and hilarious anecdote. Me and my friends started a game of Scion a while back, and our house rules allow one of your pantheon virtues to be substituted for another. The band of players includes 1 Netjer, 2 Anunna, and 1 Deva. <b>Every single one of the players independently decided to drop Order.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T09:47:10-07:00","id":125206,"title":"","content":"I have some harsher than normal penalties for having non-pantheon Virtues (your fellow Gods just feel there's something off about you...), but I have had characters choose to switch out for Order. But only if it really fit with the character concept and didn't detrimentally affect the character too severely, e.g. military officers, cops, etc. Also, characters with Justice seem to gravitate towards Order for some reason.<br /> <br /> The one that almost always gets switched in my games is Piety. I guess they all want to be defiant (towards mom or dad, et al.) without having to pay WP for it. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T11:06:50-07:00","id":125241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=125206#post125206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one that almost always gets switched in my games is Piety. I guess they all want to be defiant (towards mom or dad, et al.) without having to pay WP for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hahahaha. It probably speaks more to the types of players we hang out with. My most frequent players tend to gravitate towards Piety unless their character concepts are intentionally counter to the concept. There is one game where 3/4 players have Piety, another where 4/5 have Piety, and a third where ALL the characters have Piety.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T11:10:26-07:00","id":125243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=125241#post125241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hahahaha. It probably speaks more to the types of players we hang out with. My most frequent players tend to gravitate towards Piety unless their character concepts are intentionally counter to the concept. There is one game where 3/4 players have Piety, another where 4/5 have Piety, and a third where ALL the characters have Piety.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love Piety. Whenever I play a character, even if they're a rebel, I take Piety if the Pantheon calls for it. Love the virtue. Loooooove.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T19:44:24-07:00","id":125491,"title":"","content":"Yup, they're a rebel, right up until mom or dad tells them to do something, then they trash and moan under the WP burden adhering to the constraints of a cultural expectations of a time and place they barely understand. (Assuming of course, in said culture, you are supposed to honor and obey your parents, which is pretty standard offering for most cultures, particularly those with Piety associated).<br /> <br /> Every Virtue is a royal pain. In fact, some of the &quot;virtuous&quot; Virtues aren't. Virtuous, that is. A character without Loyalty can genuinely be loyal to their comrades easier than someone jerked around by very specific hardwired imperatives that only cover part of what actual loyalty and may actually discourage the character from following through on really helping a friend in need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T13:01:44-07:00","id":126076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=125491#post125491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup, they're a rebel, right up until mom or dad tells them to do something, then they trash and moan under the WP burden adhering to the constraints of a cultural expectations of a time and place they barely understand. (Assuming of course, in said culture, you are supposed to honor and obey your parents, which is pretty standard offering for most cultures, particularly those with Piety associated).</div> </div> </div> </div> I've ran through two games with high-piety characters and both of them weren't the golden example of children. One of them was a manipulative grifter who bargained in blackmail and seduction and had her interests aligned with her parents and her pantheon. The other was a warrior-champion a la Xena who had no qualms with spending WP to ignore a virtue that high (honestly, that character was always at low WP, but it was great fun).<br /> <br /> If someone wants to be antagonistic towards their own pantheon and actively work against them; then yes, Piety is going to be a virtue you want to keep at 1 forever and ever ... but a rebellious, independent character can have up to Piety 5 and still function. I've had players do so, and I've done it myself. Right now I've got a PC Theoi Scion son of Zeus who is about to enact the prophecy of Zeus falling to a son's hand and he's got ...3 Piety? There's gonna be huge consequences but Virtues are <b>not </b>the be-all and end-all of how a character should act. They're limitations and limitations can (and should be) overcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T14:46:02-07:00","id":126154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=125491#post125491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup, they're a rebel, right up until mom or dad tells them to do something, then they trash and moan under the WP burden adhering to the constraints of a cultural expectations of a time and place they barely understand. (Assuming of course, in said culture, you are supposed to honor and obey your parents, which is pretty standard offering for most cultures, particularly those with Piety associated).<br /> <br /> Every Virtue is a royal pain. In fact, some of the &quot;virtuous&quot; Virtues aren't. Virtuous, that is. A character without Loyalty can genuinely be loyal to their comrades easier than someone jerked around by very specific hardwired imperatives that only cover part of what actual loyalty and may actually discourage the character from following through on really helping a friend in need.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that some people run Piety like this, but, I don't believe that is a very accurate way to run Piety. RAW, it is a violation of Piety to &quot;Defy the wishes of family or a God,&quot; which can be an accurate interpretation of Piety for some Pantheons, but very much not all Pantheons. We all know that RAW is a bit iffy with a lot of things, from some dodgy mechanics, to some dodgy mythology.<br /> <br /> Piety is upholding the values of your culture, believing that your Pantheon is the greatest because you just <i>are</i>. Now, for some cultures, following the will of the Gods to the letter is an entirely acceptable expression of Piety, but not for all, not at all. A Tuatha Scion with Piety is going to have a very different Virtue then a Shen Scion with Piety, an Aesir Scion with Piety, or a Teotl Scion with Piety.<br /> <br /> The way that Piety could express itself for an Aesir Scion is that you worship the Gods, and strive with every fiber of your being to be the pinnacle of what the ancient Scandinavian (and Germanic) cultures that spawned them believed a person could be. For the Aesir, this would mean fitting into your gender role (no being like Odin and running around with women's magic), and being the best at whatever role in society you take up to be yours. Are you one of Odin's sons? You must be the greatest Prince (or son of the Chieftain) you can be. Are you a Skald? Travel to the far reaches of the earth and return with the stories of your Band. Are you a warrior? Pretty much just be Beowulf and you'll be fine.<br /> <br /> For a Tuatha Scion? Piety pretty much just means that you should be amazing. Be awesome, have no blemish on your social record. Be the greatest Druid, Bard, King, Champion, Smith, Magician, or whatever you want to be. (With a possible exception of women being Kings but the lack of women kings recorded may be because of Christianisation and the records being written three to five hundred years after Christianity arrived) If your Divine Parent shows up and goes, &quot;Hey, stop doing what you want, and do what I tell you.&quot;, just buckling to what they want would be a pretty big failure on your part. You can do what they want, if that is what <i>you</i> want. If you want to tell your Divine Parent to shove it, go nuts, but you're going to have to live with the consequences of your actions. If you did it in a manor that was incredibly brave? Standing up for what you believed in despite a God threatening to kill you? You're going to get some praise from the Fili.<br /> <br /> So, while sometimes doing just as mommy or daddy tells you is a valid expression of Piety, for example, it is accurate for the Anunna, the Gods of Mesopotamia, since Humanity was effectively created as a slave race to do things since the Lesser Gods got mad they were being used as slaves for the Greater Gods. So, until you undergo Apotheosis, you know in your very soul you are not worth as much as a God by any streach of the imagination. But, all of that is just an expression of you fitting into your role that the ancient culture that the Pantheon came from.<br /> <br /> RAW Piety is kinda silly, in that regard. Doing what the Gods tell you is <i>sometimes</i> a valid expression of Piety, but defiantly not <i>all</i> the time. You should be filling your role in this ancient culture, being the best at it, and knowing that your culture is better then all these other, clearly lesser ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T16:08:34-07:00","id":126213,"title":"","content":"Agreed.<br /> <br /> However, the comment still stands as largely relevant as the pantheons identified as having Piety as a Virtue have a high congruence to the cultures where obeying your parents is definitely a &quot;thing&quot; <br /> <br /> Except for the Tuatha. Where Piety seems a little odd as far as fit goes, because the &quot;excellence&quot; thing is sorta already covered, there's not a lot of &quot;those guys aren't like us, just a bunch of uncool barbarians, etc. Not even a lot of adherence to codes of hospitality, etc. <br /> <br /> Getting into what happens when you give non-pantheon Virtues to members of pantheons is a whole different discussion. For example, Aesir with Conviction. Since the Day of Ragnarok is inevitable and the ultimate fate of all, could an Aesir with Conviction get into a place where the Virtue is compelling him/her to do something to bring it about? Should they be focusing a chunk of their life on making sure they are ready to fulfill their appointed role on the day of?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T16:51:29-07:00","id":126256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=126213#post126213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except for the Tuatha. Where Piety seems a little odd as far as fit goes, because the &quot;excellence&quot; thing is sorta already covered, there's not a lot of &quot;those guys aren't like us, just a bunch of uncool barbarians, etc. Not even a lot of adherence to codes of hospitality, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Laws of Hospitality were a Big Deal in Ireland. Like, a Really Big Deal. I don't think we have a single example of the Tuatha themselves violating hospitality, even the Formori don't break it to attack The Dagda. A breach of hospitality was something you could legally be ostricised over, you could be satarised, it was a big deal. Bres fell from power because he didn't properly follow the laws of hospitality involving Bards. <br /> <br /> And, while there is not a lot of &quot;those people suck&quot; mentality, there is a very large, &quot;We are the most amazing&quot; mentality. I think Piety is one of the best fits for the Irish, really. I think Intellect is the biggest streach of their Virtues. I know what the writers were going for with it, they were trying to express the &quot;being a clever shit&quot; theme they have in their myths and culture, but Intellect doesn't actually express that. I would probably replace Intellect with Vengeance, since we have more examples of the Irish Gods being Vengeful rather then fufilling Intellect. Although then you get into a weird situation because while the Irish probably have Vengeance, it is not something they really approve of as a society. They had a system like the Wergild to prevent blood fueds. But, even though it is a bad thing, Lugh, The Morrigan, Aengus, Dian Cecht, they all have it for sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=126213#post126213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Getting into what happens when you give non-pantheon Virtues to members of pantheons is a whole different discussion. For example, Aesir with Conviction. Since the Day of Ragnarok is inevitable and the ultimate fate of all, could an Aesir with Conviction get into a place where the Virtue is compelling him/her to do something to bring it about? Should they be focusing a chunk of their life on making sure they are ready to fulfill their appointed role on the day of?</div> </div> </div> </div>Conviction is kinda weird since it is up to the individual to decide what their Conviction is for. Sure, you could have an Aesir who had the Conviction, &quot;Fulfill the will of Fate&quot;, but it wouldn't be mandatory for one of them. They could as much have, &quot;Fight Fate&quot; as one of their Convictions as that. You could have a Teotl without Duty and have their Conviction be &quot;Stop the Blood Sacrifices&quot;, but I wouldn't advise it. Conviction is a very character based Virtue, as Piety is a very Pantheon based one, and Harmony is a very Pantheon based one as well. (Different Pantheons will believe different things are disrupting Harmony.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T22:50:58-07:00","id":126470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/107961-order-virtue-bullshit?p=126213#post126213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except for the Tuatha. Where Piety seems a little odd as far as fit goes, because the &quot;excellence&quot; thing is sorta already covered, there's not a lot of &quot;those guys aren't like us, just a bunch of uncool barbarians, etc. Not even a lot of adherence to codes of hospitality, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ru0moPt.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}